# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A filter run stops at its own closing delimiter"

# A bare title stands as a legal filter run, and filteredtranscludeblock matches
# \{\{\{([^\}]+)\}\}\} (core/…/rules/filteredtranscludeblock.js). An unquoted run that
# eats its own }}} leaves the transclusion open and colours the rest of the file.

{{{Bare}}}
#  ^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.transclusion.filteredtranscludeblock.tiddlywiki5 meta.filter.tiddlywiki5
#      ^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.transclusion.filteredtranscludeblock.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.transclusion.filteredtranscludeblock.end.tiddlywiki5

# The line after it reads as its own construct, never as filter text.
! A heading after a bare filter run
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.heading.heading-1.tiddlywiki5 markup.heading.punctuation.definition.tiddlywiki5
#<- - meta.filter.tiddlywiki5

A paragraph after a bare filter run.
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5
#<- - meta.filter.tiddlywiki5

# The MVV display form closes on its own delimiter too (core/…/rules/mvvdisplayinline.js).
(((Bare)))
#  ^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5

! A heading after a bare MVV filter
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.heading.heading-1.tiddlywiki5 markup.heading.punctuation.definition.tiddlywiki5
#<- - meta.filter.tiddlywiki5
